\caption{\textbf{Pricing local wall-clock at a market GPU-hour rate rather than at marginal electricity raises local costs by \OWNMULTLO\ to \OWNMULTHI$\times$, and cuts the headline plan's multiplier from \LFMULT\ to \MULTAMORT.} Amortized dollars are a campaign's accelerator count $\times$ wall-clock hours $\times$ \$4.29/GPU-hour \citep{gpupricing}, over the attempts it served; the wall already reflects how many tasks ran at once (\emph{In flight}, agent time summed over attempts over the wall), so no occupancy divisor is assumed. Marginal dollars are the same campaign's measured joules at \$0.0871/kWh, so the ratio is the GPU-hour rate over the electricity one board draws in an hour. Gemma-4-31B's campaign wall was not recorded. The shaded headline row runs its first stage on the laptop of \S\ref{sec:envelope}, charged its list price over three years on the amortized basis (\S\ref{sec:measure}), and adds its unchanged provider leg to each basis's self-served legs.}
\label{tab:bases}
